{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ab84b7f16451ad83","name":"card_event_brute_force","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/events/card_event_brute_force","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BRUTE FORCE","text":"Deal 1 damage to target enemy for each unit you control above the enemy.","flavorText":"The occupation of Albania by Italy took place in April 1939 during the early stages of WWII. Italy, under the leadership of Benito Mussolini, sought to expand its influence in the Balkans and establish a puppet state in Albania. The invasion and subsequent occupation were swift and relatively uncontested. The Italian forces, led by General Alfredo Guzzoni, launched a combined air, land, and naval assault on Albania. The Italian military employed overwhelming force, including aerial bombardments, naval shelling, and ground offensives, to quickly overpower the Albanian defenses which only had 8,000 soldiers, 5 aircraft and 3 torpedo boats at their disposal. Facing overwhelming odds, the Albanian army, led by King Zog I, was unable to mount a significant defense and was forced to retreat. Following the occupation, Italy installed a puppet regime led by Shefqet Vërlaci, who was declared the Prime Minister of Albania. However, the Italian occupation of Albania was met with resistance from various Albanian nationalist and communist groups. The National Liberation Movement, led by Enver Hoxha, emerged as a significant force opposing the Italian occupation. The Italian occupation of Albania lasted until September 1943 when Italy surrendered to the Allied forces. After Italy's capitulation, Germany took control of Albania and continued the occupation until the end of the war. The occupation had a significant impact on Albania's political and social landscape, fueling nationalist sentiments and setting the stage for the country's subsequent struggle for independence and communist rule under Enver Hoxha.","faction":"Italy","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_brute_force","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_brute_force_title","SourceString":"BRUTE FORCE","LocalizedString":"BRUTE FORCE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_brute_force_text","SourceString":"Deal 1 damage to target enemy for each unit you control above the enemy.","LocalizedString":"Deal 1 damage to target enemy for each unit you control above the enemy."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_brute_force_history","SourceString":"The occupation of Albania by Italy took place in April 1939 during the early stages of WWII. Italy, under the leadership of Benito Mussolini, sought to expand its influence in the Balkans and establish a puppet state in Albania. The invasion and subsequent occupation were swift and relatively uncontested. The Italian forces, led by General Alfredo Guzzoni, launched a combined air, land, and naval assault on Albania. The Italian military employed overwhelming force, including aerial bombardments, naval shelling, and ground offensives, to quickly overpower the Albanian defenses which only had 8,000 soldiers, 5 aircraft and 3 torpedo boats at their disposal. Facing overwhelming odds, the Albanian army, led by King Zog I, was unable to mount a significant defense and was forced to retreat. Following the occupation, Italy installed a puppet regime led by Shefqet Vërlaci, who was declared the Prime Minister of Albania. However, the Italian occupation of Albania was met with resistance from various Albanian nationalist and communist groups. The National Liberation Movement, led by Enver Hoxha, emerged as a significant force opposing the Italian occupation. The Italian occupation of Albania lasted until September 1943 when Italy surrendered to the Allied forces. After Italy's capitulation, Germany took control of Albania and continued the occupation until the end of the war. The occupation had a significant impact on Albania's political and social landscape, fueling nationalist sentiments and setting the stage for the country's subsequent struggle for independence and communist rule under Enver Hoxha.","LocalizedString":"The occupation of Albania by Italy took place in April 1939 during the early stages of WWII. Italy, under the leadership of Benito Mussolini, sought to expand its influence in the Balkans and establish a puppet state in Albania. The invasion and subsequent occupation were swift and relatively uncontested. The Italian forces, led by General Alfredo Guzzoni, launched a combined air, land, and naval assault on Albania. The Italian military employed overwhelming force, including aerial bombardments, naval shelling, and ground offensives, to quickly overpower the Albanian defenses which only had 8,000 soldiers, 5 aircraft and 3 torpedo boats at their disposal. Facing overwhelming odds, the Albanian army, led by King Zog I, was unable to mount a significant defense and was forced to retreat. Following the occupation, Italy installed a puppet regime led by Shefqet Vërlaci, who was declared the Prime Minister of Albania. However, the Italian occupation of Albania was met with resistance from various Albanian nationalist and communist groups. The National Liberation Movement, led by Enver Hoxha, emerged as a significant force opposing the Italian occupation. The Italian occupation of Albania lasted until September 1943 when Italy surrendered to the Allied forces. After Italy's capitulation, Germany took control of Albania and continued the occupation until the end of the war. The occupation had a significant impact on Albania's political and social landscape, fueling nationalist sentiments and setting the stage for the country's subsequent struggle for independence and communist rule under Enver Hoxha."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Tactical_Bomber_Attack'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Tactical_Bomber_Attack.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/Spring2023Candidates/t_italian_air_order_xxx.t_italian_air_order_xxx","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/BRUTE_FORCE.BRUTE_FORCE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":350.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_brute_force_photo","SourceString":"Italian troops disembarking at an Albanian port, 1939.","LocalizedString":"Italian troops disembarking at an Albanian port, 1939."},"isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"cardsToDestroy","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"},{"name":"myUnitCount","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"enemyUnitCount","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_brute_force_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetOppositeSide_oppositeSide","type":"ESideEnum","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_EqualEqual_ByteByte_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"body":[{"op":"Context","at":0,"object":{"op":"Variable","name":"cardFunction","type":"ACardFunctionsStub*","scope":"member","sourceOp":"InstanceVariable"},"value":{"op":"Loc